<title>FRANCE: Synthelabo seeks acquisitions in Europe.</title>
<headline>Synthelabo seeks acquisitions in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceuticals company Synthelabo, controlled by L'Oreal, aims to nearly double sales by the year 2000 and expects half the growth to come from acquisitions, chairman Herve Guerin said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He told an analysts' meeting that the company aimed to increase sales to between 18 and 20 billion francs by the year 2000 from 10.4 billion in 1996 and &quot;half would come from external growth&quot; in Europe.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
